+### Worker git push and pull requests
+
+This is **not** automated by widening the kickoff workflow `permissions:` or by installing the Cursor GitHub App. Self-hosted AgentCore workers do **not** receive Cursor’s GitHub App token and do **not** inherit Actions `GITHUB_TOKEN`. `autoCreatePR` uses whatever HTTPS credentials are already on the worker VM.
+
+A running session also does **not** pick up adapter or IAM changes. After you add the git-token secret, you must `make agentcore-ecr-build-push`, `terraform apply` so the runtime gets `CURSOR_GIT_TOKEN_SECRET_ID`, and start a **new** session.
+
+**1. Create a fine-grained GitHub PAT** (Settings → Developer settings → Fine-grained tokens) for the application repo (`WORKER_REPOSITORY_URL`), not this cookbook:
+
+| Permission | Access | Why |
+|---|---|---|
+| Metadata | Read | Automatic |
+| Contents | Read and write | `git fetch` / `git push` |
+| Pull requests | Read and write | Open and update agent PRs |
+| Workflows | Read and write | Required if the agent edits `.github/workflows/*.yml` |
+
+Resource owner and repository must match the app the worker clones. Do not put the token in git, Terraform variables, or `config.yaml`.
+
+**2. Store it in Secrets Manager** as JSON (plaintext also works):
+
+```json
+{"CURSOR_GIT_TOKEN":"github_pat_..."}
+```
+
+Default secret name: `cursor-agentcore-worker-git-token`.
+
+```bash
+export CURSOR_GIT_TOKEN=github_pat_...
+make agentcore-put-git-token-secret
+```
+
+If you already created that secret by hand, set `CREATE_CURSOR_GIT_TOKEN_SECRET=false` in `.env` so Terraform looks it up instead of trying to create it again.
+
+**3. Grant the runtime execution role `secretsmanager:GetSecretValue`** on that secret ARN and pass the ARN into the adapter:
+
+```text
+CURSOR_GIT_TOKEN_SECRET_ID=<secret ARN>
+```
+
+`make agentcore-terraform-apply` does both. The adapter also tries the default secret name when the env var is unset.
+
+**4. Publish a new worker image and start a new session.** The adapter fetches the token at boot, writes `/usr/local/bin/git-credential-github-env`, and exports `CURSOR_GIT_TOKEN` to `agent worker`. A missing or unreadable git secret is logged and is not fatal — the worker still registers — but `git push` and `autoCreatePR` will fail until the token is readable.
+
+**5. Verify on a claimed worker:**
+
+```bash
+# adapter logs should include: loaded worker git token from Secrets Manager
+git ls-remote --heads origin
+git push -u origin HEAD
+```
+
+`git ls-remote` can succeed on a public repo without write access. `git push` is the real check.
+
+Copy [`github/WORKER_GIT.md`](github/WORKER_GIT.md) into the application repo so agents have the same contract. The application-repo helpers (`.github/scripts/configure-worker-git.sh`) are a fallback for images that do not yet fetch the token at boot.
+
