@@ -0,0 +1,74 @@
+# Worker git credentials (so agents can open PRs)
+
+Self-hosted Cursor / AgentCore workers **do not** receive Cursor’s GitHub App token and **do not** see the Actions `GITHUB_TOKEN`. Push and `autoCreatePR` use whatever credentials are already on the worker VM. That is Cursor’s self-hosted design.
+
+Widening `.github/workflows/cursor-agent-in-progress.yml` `permissions:` (for example `contents: write`) does **not** let an agent open a PR. That token exists only in the kickoff job, which never has the agent’s commits.
+
+Copy this file into the **application** repository (not cursor-cookbook). The adapter in the worker image is what loads the token at boot.
+
+## What to put on the AgentCore worker
+
+Create a **fine-grained PAT** (GitHub → Settings → Developer settings → Fine-grained tokens) for the application repo in `WORKER_REPOSITORY_URL`:
+
+| Permission | Access |
+|---|---|
+| Contents | Read and write |
+| Pull requests | Read and write |
+| Workflows | Read and write (needed if the agent edits `.github/workflows/*.yml`) |
+| Metadata | Read (automatic) |
+
+Do **not** put this token in git or `config.yaml`.
+
+Store it in Secrets Manager. Default name: `cursor-agentcore-worker-git-token`. JSON (preferred) or plaintext:
+
+```json
+{"CURSOR_GIT_TOKEN":"github_pat_..."}
+```
+
+From `self-hosted-cloud-agent/agentcore`:
+
+```bash
+export CURSOR_GIT_TOKEN=github_pat_...
+make agentcore-put-git-token-secret
+make agentcore-terraform-apply
+make agentcore-ecr-build-push
+```
+
+Terraform sets `CURSOR_GIT_TOKEN_SECRET_ID` on the runtime and grants the execution role `secretsmanager:GetSecretValue` on that ARN. If the secret already exists, set `CREATE_CURSOR_GIT_TOKEN_SECRET=false` before apply.
+
+The adapter fetches the token at startup, installs `/usr/local/bin/git-credential-github-env`, and exports `CURSOR_GIT_TOKEN` to `agent worker`. A missing secret is logged and is not fatal; `git push` then fails.
+
+A **running** session does not pick up a new image or runtime env. Start a new session after the apply and image push.
+
+## Fallback on an older image
+
+If the live image does not yet fetch the git token, load it in the claimed workspace:
+
+```bash
+.github/scripts/load-worker-git-token.sh
+```
+
+Aliases the helper also accepts: `GH_TOKEN`, `GH_WORKER_TOKEN`.
+
+## Check
+
+On a claimed worker:
+
+```bash
+git ls-remote --heads origin
+git push -u origin HEAD
+```
+
+`git ls-remote` can succeed on a public repo **without** write access. `git push` is the real check. Adapter logs should include `loaded worker git token from Secrets Manager`.
+
+## What will not work
+
+- Raising the kickoff workflow’s `GITHUB_TOKEN` scopes
+- Expanding `GH_PROJECT_TOKEN` **only** as an Actions secret (it is not injected into AgentCore)
+- Relying on Cursor hosted-VM App tokens — those are not injected into self-hosted workers
+
+You **can** reuse the same PAT as `GH_PROJECT_TOKEN` **if** you also install it on the worker and add Contents + Pull requests write. Projects: Read stays required for the 5-minute scan.
+
+## Cursor team-pool minting (optional alternative)
+
+If you switch from AgentCore to Cursor’s `agent worker --pool` with `--mint-github-token` / `--clone-git-repos`, a team admin can enable GitHub token minting in the Cloud Agents dashboard. That still does not apply to this AgentCore image until the worker is started that way.
